# Battery

The Battery report answers the question "how do the batteries of my devices
charge and run down?". It uses the status reports that your uploader app sends,
for example from your phone or your pump.

<Video id="battery" />

## What it shows

### One card for each device

Each device that sends status reports gets its own card. The badge at the top
right of the card shows the battery level now. The colour of the battery icon
shows the status: normal, warning or urgent.

Each card shows:

- **Current**: the battery level now. A lightning icon shows that the battery
  is charging.
- **Readings**: the number of battery reports in the period.
- **Avg level** and **Range**: the average battery level, and the lowest and
  highest level.
- **Charge Patterns**: the number of charge **Cycles**, and how long the
  battery lasted after a charge: **Avg life**, **Longest** and **Shortest**.
- **Time Distribution**: the part of the period that the battery was **Above
  80%**, between **30% - 80%**, and **Below 30%**.
- The number of warnings and critical events, if there were any.

### Recent Charge Cycles

The list shows the last 10 charge cycles. Each one shows the device, when it
charged and from which level to which level, and how long the charge lasted.
A cycle that has not finished shows **In Progress**.

## How to use it

The report opens on the last 7 days. One week shows only a few charges. To see
more:

1. At the top of the report, select the date range.
2. Select **30 Days**.
3. Select **Apply Filters**. The report loads again for 30 days.
4. Look at **Range** and **Time Distribution** to see how low each battery went.

If you have more than one device, select a device name above the cards to show
only that device. Select **All Devices** to show all of them again. To load the
latest data, select **Refresh**.

## Good to know

- If the report shows **No Battery Data Available**, make sure that your
  uploader app sends device status data to Nocturne.
